id=a52sxq_fingerprint
name=Galaxy A52s 5G UDFPS sensor position access and FOD HBM
author=kusti420
description=FingerprintService (system_server), SystemUI and AODService read the under-display sensor position from /sys/class/fingerprint/fingerprint/position. That path goes through a plain "sysfs" symlink which Android 17 policy only lets hal_fingerprint follow (and genfscon can't relabel sysfs symlinks on 5.4), so the framework never learns the sensor area and never sends the touch-down request (sehRequest 22) to the HAL: enrollment sits at 0% while the sensor waits (fpop 100020). Point all of them at the real node /sys/devices/virtual/fingerprint/fingerprint/position (sysfs_ss_writable, readable by system_server and platform_app). Optical FOD HBM: stock One UI enters finger-mask HBM when the QTI composer sees a layer whose buffer carries Samsung's gralloc usage bit 34 (SurfaceFlinger's 'Fingerprint Indisplay Layer', absent from the Fold8 SurfaceFlinger), so BiometricSetting's UdfpsMaskWindow attaches such a 16x16 alpha-0.01 layer while the mask is shown and writes the HBM level to mask_brightness.
